: {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AtPWyLx2YoMq4iy46nuL9T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-fin-212-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012VJ2WJnXEsX1NKqypckEW5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019oJFx69EDJmTvou3Tnij6s", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, while its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212.\n\nThis change switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. With this change, `2.665` rounds to `2.66`.\n\nCI: ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug that was breaking the nightly build. CI passed, and I opened pull request #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded halves up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). Its own description and `tests/test_money.py` both require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212, so 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed that one line to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}